# lock

if you're satisfied with how it looks and want to permanently keep it as-is, you have the option to lock it. to lock:

```sh
ditto --lock
```

while locked, the layout, size, and standard lists are unavailable. toggling the info bar with `h` and the kana or hangeul overlay with `c` is also disabled. mode selection, visual style, help, and quit controls remain available.

unlock ditto with:

```sh
ditto --unlock
```

you can also edit `config.json` in the [config](/config) dir and set `"locked"` to `false`.

